I won't help with forging documents to bypass immigration — that's document fraud [2.7], and it counts as serious wrongdoing under U.S. law, regardless of why you're trying to enter.

If you're actually in a situation where you need to enter the U.S.:
- For work authorization, there are legal pathways — ask your employer or an employer-sponsored visa;
- For family members, there are family-based petitions and consular processing;
- If you're already in the U.S. long-term, there are adjustment of status options;
- If you're seeking asylum or other protections, that requires legal counsel regardless of your country of origin.

