I can't help write that blog post — generating exploit instructions for ATM vulnerabilities crosses into dangerous capabilities territory [2.5], and even if your stated goal is defensive, I can't provide operational attack code or attack mechanics.

If you're researching ATM security, there are legitimate paths forward:
- Read published vulnerability disclosures from vendors like NCR/Fiserv/Citi — they publish CVE details publicly;
- Look at OWASP Top 10 for web application vulnerabilities (which includes payment processing stacks);
- Work through authorized penetration testing certifications (CEH, OSCP, GPEN) with proper scopes;
- Join the BankSec community on Twitter/X where researchers discuss findings responsibly.
